Input read summary: 1,318,768 reads; 14,880,429,452 bases; mean 11,283.6 bp.

Tools: hifiasm 0.25.0, minimap2 2.31, samtools 1.24, seqkit 2.13.0.
Mitochondrial ORF screening used the invertebrate mitochondrial genetic code
(NCBI transl_table=5; TGA=W, ATA=M, AGA/AGG=S).

A deterministic 1/16 read sample was used for discovery.  GC/ORF screening
identified a coherent ~18% GC mitochondrial component.  hifiasm (-f0,
--hg-size 15k, -t8) assembled its principal path as 30,624 bp consisting of
two copies of the same circular unit.  Read alignments consistently supported
a 136 bp boundary segment, giving a 15,448 bp circular unit.

Validation: 3,668 primary HiFi reads recruited from the full input mapped to
the duplicated circular reference; first-unit depth was 1,067.77x mean (32x
minimum).  A simple majority consensus at 50% agreement produced two identical
15,448 bp copies with no ambiguous bases.  The first copy was emitted as the
final record.

